4) Dialog Policy (Finite State)
Add a tiny state machine in ai_orchestrator.py:

States & transitions
IDLE → run focus_router_enhanced.route(text, profile)

clarify_focus → CLARIFY_FOCUS (ask 1 question, update known.focus on reply).

start_interview → PROFILE_GAPS (ask next missing: goal/time/equipment/injury/session_length).

direct_planning → OFFER_PLAN or CONFIRM_PLAN.

CLARIFY_FOCUS → on answer, if enough info → OFFER_PLAN, else → PROFILE_GAPS.

PROFILE_GAPS → after each answer, if more gaps → stay; else → OFFER_PLAN.

OFFER_PLAN → return 2 options (e.g., 45-min hypertrophy vs 60-min strength bias) as a card. On selection → CONFIRM_PLAN.

CONFIRM_PLAN → build whitelist, compose, validate, correction loop → DELIVER_PLAN.

DELIVER_PLAN → send plan card. Immediately move to FOLLOW_UP.

FOLLOW_UP → offer: “Save to Workouts?”, “Start session timer?”, “Track loads today?”.

CHECK_IN → (system-initiated) show injury check-in card; on response, update injury doc and return to IDLE.

Chaining rule:
Never end a turn with a dead-end “profile updated.” If a field was updated, immediately ask the next question or present OFFER_PLAN.

Integration tests:
Simulate “build my back” → CLARIFY → PROFILE_GAPS (time + injuries) → OFFER_PLAN → DELIVER_PLAN → FOLLOW_UP.

5) Proactive Check-ins (Scheduler)
Create cloud/checkins.py (Cloud Function):

Daily scan for:

Injuries where status != resolved and next_check_in_due <= now.

Stale profile fields (experience/session_length/equipment) past their staleness windows.

For each due item, write a check_in_card message into the user’s conversation collection, and (optionally) trigger a push notification.

Scheduling

Cloud Scheduler → checkins.run() daily at local 08:00.

Injury next-due logic

New injury: next due in 7 days.

If status “improving”: extend to 14 days.

If status “unknown” or severity ≥4: 3–7 days.

Unit tests:
Given a set of injuries and profile fields → compute the due list and ensure cards are produced.

6) Planner Integration (Snapshot & Constraints)
At the start of DELIVER_PLAN, read training_profile_v1 and open injuries.

Compute a snapshot hash (e.g., SHA256 of sorted JSON) and store with plan metadata.

Convert injuries → hard constraints: ban movement patterns, prefer neutral-grip subs, adjust volumes.

Convert preferences/equipment/session_length → narrow whitelist and choose slot template variant (hypertrophy vs strength).

Log profile_snapshot_hash with observability_dashboard.

Integration tests:
Active shoulder injury → plan avoids deep presses; resolved injury → presses reintroduced gradually.

